# D-22 (steps/defects.md): L2 spec 18.2 gives `@array[i]` address arithmetic
# a meaning ("follow the C machine contract"), but l2trans has no
# expression-type inference to keep a pointer result from silently reaching
# a numeric target (this exact shape, ex-address_array_element_sum.lm2,
# used to compile and return a pointer value as `int` with only a gcc
# warning -Wint-conversion to show it). Refused outright until that type
# tracking exists; `@ buf[i]` alone (D-21) is unaffected.
fn: sum_address () int
    []: int buf 3
    buf[0]: 1
    buf[1]: 2
    buf[2]: 3
    return: @ buf[0] + buf[1] + buf[2]
end: sum_address
return: 0
